      "heading": "Find every full moon through 2027.",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "opposition is a single computable instant — the times above — though the Moon looks essentially full for a night before and after. Because it is an opposition, the pairing of signs is fixed: a full moon in Capricorn can only happen while the Sun is in Cancer , and so on around the wheel. The names are older than the astrology columns that borrowed them. North American almanacs, drawing on Algonquian and colonial seasonal tradition, tied each month’s moon to the working year: wolves in the January cold, sap worms in March, the buck’s new antlers in July. They are calendar poetry, not sky data — the computed column is the sign and degree, which is what an astrologer actually reads. Where that degree lands in your chart takes a birth chart ; the monthly horoscopes track each lunation as it"
