      "heading": "The astrology glossary.",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "These fifteen explain most of what you will meet in a first birth chart. 01 Birth chart (natal chart) A snapshot of where the planets appeared at the moment you were born. 02 Big three Your Sun, Moon, and rising signs—the three quickest entry points into a birth chart. 03 Rising sign The sign rising on the eastern horizon at your birth; it depends on an accurate time and place. 04 House system A method for dividing a birth chart into twelve areas of life. 05 Whole-sign houses A house system in which each zodiac sign becomes one complete 30° house. 06 Placidus A house system that uses your exact birth time and location to create houses of different sizes. 07 House One of twelve chart areas describing where a theme tends to show up in life. 08 Aspect A measured angle between two chart points that astrologers read as a relationship between them. 09 Conjunction A 0° aspect that"
