      "text": "Read the Aries guide → Ascendant # Chart anatomy The exact point rising on the eastern horizon, often shortened to ASC. Precise definition The ascendant is the ecliptic degree rising on the eastern horizon at a specific time and place. It anchors the first house and supplies the rising sign; without a known birth time, this site omits the angles and houses. Descendant = Ascendant + 180° Related Rising sign · Descendant · First house · Angle Calculate the ascendant → Aspect # Aspects A measured angle between two chart points that astrologers read as a relationship between them. Precise definition An aspect is a recognized angular relationship between two chart positions. This site calculates the five major aspects and reports the distance from each exact angle as its orb. Related Major aspect · Angular separation · Orb Read the aspect guides → B Bi-wheel # A bi-wheel draws two charts on"
