      "heading": "The astrology glossary.",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "Use the synastry calculator → Conjunction # Aspects A 0° aspect that concentrates two parts of the chart in the same place. Precise definition A conjunction places two chart bodies together at the same zodiac longitude. Its exact angular separation is 0°, and the engine treats closeness as concentration rather than ease or strain by itself. Exact 0° · natal orb ≤ 8° · with Sun or Moon ≤ 10° Related Aspect · Orb · Applying aspect · Separating aspect Read the conjunction guide → Contraparallel # A contraparallel joins two bodies at the same declination on opposite sides of the celestial equator, mirrored across it, and traditional practice reads it much as it reads an opposition. Like the parallel it is invisible on a chart wheel, which plots zodiac longitude and not declination. This site marks contraparallels within 1° of exact, or 1.5° when the Sun or Moon is one of the pair. Mirrored"
