      "text": "declinations within 1° · 1.5° with Sun or Moon Related Parallel · Declination · Opposition · Aspect Read how contraparallels work → Cusp # Chart anatomy The boundary where one sign or house ends and the next begins. Precise definition A cusp is a boundary, usually between houses or between zodiac signs in date-based shorthand. A computed sign changes only at an exact ingress, while house cusps depend on the selected house system. Related Ingress · House system · Zodiac sign Check a birthday boundary → D Day sign # A day sign belongs to the outward-facing half of the zodiac’s alternating polarity. Aries, Gemini, Leo, Libra, Sagittarius, and Aquarius make up this group. Related Night sign · Polarity Decan # A decan is one of three equal divisions within a zodiac sign. This site uses ten-degree triplicity decans and assigns their rulers from the classical table. Three decans per sign ·"
