      "locale": "en",
      "text": "10° each Related Degree · Zodiac sign · Classical ruler Look up birthday decans → Declination # Declination is angular distance north or south of the celestial equator, which is a different reference plane from the ecliptic and so a different measurement from ecliptic latitude. A chart wheel does not carry it: the wheel plots zodiac longitude only. The dimensional view on the birth-chart page computes declination for the ten Sun-through-Pluto bodies and draws the circles they ride. Bounded by the obliquity of the ecliptic, ±23.44° Related Ecliptic latitude · Out of bounds · Parallel · Contraparallel Read how declination works → Degree # Chart anatomy A unit for locating something precisely around the 360° chart circle. Precise definition A degree is one three-hundred-and-sixtieth of a circle and the basic unit used for chart longitude. Sign degree describes a position within its"
