      "locale": "en",
      "text": "season See upcoming lunar eclipses → Lunar nodes # The lunar nodes are the two points where the Moon’s orbit crosses the ecliptic. This site calculates the true North Node and derives the exactly opposite South Node, but excludes both from natal and synastry aspect detection. Related North Node · South Node · True node · Ecliptic Read the node method → Lunation # A lunation is the cycle from one new moon to the next, or a particular new or full moon within that cycle. Eclipses are lunations that occur close enough to the lunar nodes for the Sun, Earth, and Moon to align. Related New moon · Full moon · Eclipse · Lunar nodes Check the lunar cycle → M Major aspect # Major aspect is the collective label for conjunction, sextile, square, trine, and opposition. Those are the only aspect types used by this site’s natal and synastry calculations. Related Conjunction · Sextile · Square · Trine ·"
