      "title": "Astrology Glossary — 145 Terms Defined",
      "heading": "The astrology glossary.",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "Applying aspect · Separating aspect Read the opposition guide → Orb # Aspects How far an aspect is from exact; a smaller orb means a tighter aspect. Precise definition An orb is the distance between an aspect’s current separation and its exact angle. This site uses aspect-specific limits for natal charts and a 3° limit for active transits. Active transit orb ≤ 3° Related Aspect · Exact aspect · Transit Read active transits → Out of bounds # A body is out of bounds when its declination passes ±23.44°, further north or south of the celestial equator than the Sun itself ever travels. The Moon and Mercury reach it most often, Venus and Mars less so, and the Sun never can, because that limit is the Sun’s own path. The dimensional view on the birth-chart page marks any body outside the bounds circles. Out of bounds when |declination| &gt; 23.44° Related Declination · Ecliptic · Moon Read how"
