      "title": "Astrology Glossary — 145 Terms Defined",
      "heading": "The astrology glossary.",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "out of bounds works → Outer planets # Outer planets is the astrological grouping for Uranus, Neptune, and Pluto. Their slow motion makes sign placements broadly generational, while house placement and exact aspects make their role more specific to one chart. Related Uranus · Neptune · Pluto · Placement Read the planet guides → P Parallel # A parallel joins two bodies at the same declination on the same side of the celestial equator, and traditional practice reads it much as it reads a conjunction. Because it measures height above the equator rather than position round the zodiac, a parallel can hold between bodies that stand half the wheel apart and show no longitude aspect at all. This site marks parallels within 1° of exact, or 1.5° when the Sun or Moon is one of the pair. Same-side declinations within 1° · 1.5° with Sun or Moon Related Contraparallel · Declination · Conjunction ·"
