      "heading": "The astrology glossary.",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "houses → Planet # Planet is the general chart label for a moving body whose zodiac position is calculated, even though astrology conventionally includes the Sun and Moon in the same list. This site calculates positions for the Sun through Pluto and both lunar nodes, and does not calculate Chiron or asteroids. Related Luminary · Personal planets · Outer planets · Lunar nodes Read the planet guides → Pluto # Pluto is the chart body associated here with power, compulsion, elimination, and slow structural change. It is used as Scorpio’s modern ruler while Mars remains the sign’s classical ruler. Related Outer planets · Scorpio · Modern ruler Read the Pluto guide → Polar fallback # Polar fallback is the switch from Placidus to whole-sign houses where the Placidus cusp calculation cannot resolve. This site applies it above 66° absolute latitude and also if circumpolar cusp math degenerates."
