      "heading": "The astrology glossary.",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "Fallback when |latitude| &gt; 66° or cusp math is undefined Related Placidus · Whole-sign houses · House system Read the house-system options → Polarity # Polarity divides the signs into alternating day and night groups, also called positive and negative in some texts. This site uses the day and night labels to avoid treating either half as better or worse. Related Day sign · Night sign · Zodiac sign Compare sign polarities → Precession # Precession is the slow change in the orientation of Earth’s rotational axis, which shifts the equinoxes relative to the stars. It is the reason tropical and sidereal zodiac frames do not stay aligned. Related Tropical zodiac · Sidereal zodiac · Ecliptic Read the calculation method → Progression # Timing A symbolic timing technique that advances a birth chart by a set rule. Precise definition A progression advances a natal chart by a symbolic timing"
