      "locale": "en",
      "text": "rule rather than using the sky positions of the target date directly. This site does not calculate progressed charts. Related Transit · Return · Birth chart (natal chart) Q Quadrant # A quadrant is one of four chart regions bounded by the ascendant–descendant and midheaven–IC axes. Quadrant house systems such as Placidus subdivide those regions into three houses each. Related Angle · Placidus · House system R Retrograde loop # A retrograde loop is the apparent path through a section of zodiac longitude as a body slows, reverses, and later resumes direct motion. It can create two or three exact contacts to the same natal point within one broader transit. Related Retrograde motion · Station · Exact aspect · Transit See retrograde periods → Retrograde motion # Timing A period when a planet appears to move backward from Earth; it has not reversed its orbit. Precise definition Retrograde"
