      "heading": "The astrology glossary.",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "motion means a body’s apparent geocentric zodiac longitude is decreasing for a time, even though the body has not reversed its physical orbit. The loop can carry a transit across the same natal point more than once. Related Direct motion · Station · Retrograde loop · Transit See retrograde periods → Return # A return occurs when a transiting body reaches the same zodiac longitude it held in a natal chart. Retrograde motion can produce multiple exact crossings, which remain separate return instants. Related Solar return · Saturn return · Transit · Retrograde loop Calculate a Saturn return → Rising sign # Chart anatomy The sign rising on the eastern horizon at your birth; it depends on an accurate time and place. Precise definition The rising sign is the tropical sign containing the ascendant. It changes with local time and place, so a date alone cannot establish it. Related Ascendant ·"
