      "text": "Chart ruler · Big three Calculate the rising sign → Rulership # Rulership is the convention that assigns one or more planets to each zodiac sign. This site displays both modern and classical rulers and uses the classical table for chart rulers and decans. Related Modern ruler · Classical ruler · Chart ruler Compare rulership tables → S Sagittarius # Sagittarius is the ninth tropical sign, spanning 240° through just under 270° of zodiac longitude. It is a mutable fire day sign ruled by Jupiter in both modern and classical tables. Related Fire · Mutable · Jupiter · Ninth house Read the Sagittarius guide → Saturn # Saturn is the chart body associated here with limits, structure, duty, delay, craft, and accountability. Its natal placement supplies the longitude used to calculate an exact Saturn return. Related Saturn return · Return · Placement Read the Saturn guide → Saturn return # A"
