      "title": "Capricorn: dates, personality, compatibility & what the Sea-Goat really means",
      "heading": "Capricorn",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "hooves for the mountain, tail for the deep water. Practical on the surface, with far more going on underneath than anyone is shown. You don’t need to believe the sky causes any of this to find the archetype useful. Capricorn is a 2,500-year-old shorthand for a recognizable kind of person: the one who plays the long game. Personality The core Capricorn pattern is endurance — the long game played as a way of life. A result ten years away feels as real to Capricorn as this afternoon feels to everyone else, and that changes every decision: hard now and worth it later beats easy now, every single time. What reads as ambition from the outside rarely feels like hunger from the inside. It feels like inevitability — of course the good things take years. The Goat never expected otherwise, and packed accordingly. That patience comes with the zodiac’s driest sense of"
