      "text": "trip that becomes the year’s best story and is told accordingly. Even rest has a little theater in it, and honestly runs better for it. The generosity is theatrical in the best sense. Birthdays get remembered at scale, the celebration arrives organized and lit, praise is delivered in public, where it counts double. This is the friend who makes an ordinary Tuesday feel like a premiere, and it gives that way because that is how it wants the world to feel. The growth edge Jupiter’s excess speaks the local language, and Leo’s dialect is the spotlight. The story of the thing swells past the thing; generosity starts keeping a quiet list of insufficient thank-yous; growth nobody witnessed begins to feel like growth that didn’t happen. At full inflation, applause stops being the reward and becomes the evidence — no clap,"
