      "text": "has visible mechanics: it walks in expecting the room to warm up, and rooms tend to meet an expectation carried that well. Add an instinct for occasions — knowing when a moment deserves to be made bigger — and the record fills with what looks like fortune and is mostly warmth plus timing. How often is Jupiter in Leo? About one year in every twelve. Jupiter spends close to a year in each sign, sometimes split across two visits when a retrograde carries it back over the boundary, and the computed windows on this page list the exact dates. Is this your Jupiter? The house Jupiter occupies says where the appetite points — that takes your birth time. Get your free birth chart ↗ Jupiter through the signs ← Cancer All placements Virgo → More in Leo ☉ Sun ☽ Moon ☿ Mercury ♀ Venus ♂ Mars ♄ Saturn ♅ Uranus ♆ Neptune ♇ Pluto"
