      "text": "the expectation does its own recruiting. The famous luck runs on reciprocity. Credit gets shared accurately, introductions get made without a running tally, both sides of a dispute get heard so thoroughly that both later speak well of the referee. People repeat the name of whoever made them look good last time, and this placement makes people look good almost structurally. Growth in company The arenas are shared ones. Study goes best at a seminar table — a co-author, a debate partner, a standing reading group — and leans toward subjects with two sides or good proportions: law, design, ethics, art and its history. Travel wants company and beauty in roughly equal measure — the city chosen for its architecture, the museum day that must be debriefed over dinner to fully count. Even the solo trip gets arranged so that people"
