      "locale": "en",
      "text": "Placements ♃ Jupiter in Pisces Classical standing domicile In plain English Domicile A traditional dignity label meaning a planet is in a sign it rules. A dignity is a traditional description of support, not a score for whether a placement is good or bad. Learn more about Domicile → — the planet in its own sign, running on home rules No fence has ever held this appetite, chiefly because it has never once noticed a fence. Jupiter in Pisces grows in every direction at the same time — outward toward strangers, inward toward the imagination — and keeps no map of where it has already given. How it shows up Jupiter marks where you expect things to work out, and in Pisces the expectation is oceanic: somehow, for everyone, eventually. The tradition gave Jupiter this sign long before telescopes added Neptune to the conversation, and the fit still"
