      "text": "exit is nearest — because a boundless appetite eventually needs somewhere to not feel everything. The mature version builds a container, and the ocean turns out to like one. The practice with a schedule, the generosity with a floor, the no that keeps next month’s yes possible. Edges don’t shrink this placement; they are what let it pour somewhere on purpose. Where the water goes is a house question — run your birth chart to see what this Jupiter keeps filling. Asked and answered What does Jupiter in Pisces mean? Jupiter marks where you expect things to work out; Pisces removes the boundaries from the expectation. Growth arrives through imagination, compassion, and the interior life, and generosity flows without much tracking of where it went. The confidence is quiet and nearly bottomless. Is Jupiter in Pisces a good placement? It’s one of"
