      "heading": "Jupiter in Sagittarius",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "Placements ♃ Jupiter in Sagittarius Classical standing domicile In plain English Domicile A traditional dignity label meaning a planet is in a sign it rules. A dignity is a traditional description of support, not a score for whether a placement is good or bad. Learn more about Domicile → — the planet in its own sign, running on home rules Of the twelve signs Jupiter passes through, this is one of two with its name on the door. In Sagittarius nothing about the planet needs converting — the appetite for distance, meaning, and the next threshold arrives at full strength and idles badly. How it shows up Jupiter marks where you assume the door opens, and in Sagittarius every door is assumed to be a trailhead. Confidence comes easiest at range: the unfamiliar country, the enormous question, the room where a worldview is being argued and someone really should take"
