      "heading": "Mercury in Capricorn",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "decoder — some colleagues spend years feeling merely tolerated by someone who considers them excellent. The growth edge Spending words on purpose. The compression is real efficiency, but relationships run on a little redundancy — the extra sentence that says how, the compliment delivered at full length once a quarter, the reasoning offered before the verdict so people can join it rather than receive it. The other work is entertaining an unproven idea for ten full minutes before demanding its evidence; some of the best ones arrive without references. Even review season gets managed here: this placement treats the three Mercury retrograde windows a year as scheduled maintenance — the calendar goes in the calendar — which is, in fairness, exactly how to use them. Run your birth"
