      "heading": "Mercury in Gemini",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "Placements ☿ Mercury in Gemini Classical standing domicile In plain English Domicile A traditional dignity label meaning a planet is in a sign it rules. A dignity is a traditional description of support, not a score for whether a placement is good or bad. Learn more about Domicile → — the planet in its own sign, running on home rules Mercury rules Gemini, and you can hear the home-field advantage inside one sentence — the pivot, the pun, the parenthesis that lands on its feet. Between thought and speech there is no friction at all, which is the gift and, eventually, the bill. How it shows up Mercury runs the chart’s information layer, and Gemini is one of the two signs where it works from home. Thinking happens out loud and in motion: this placement talks to find out what"
