      "heading": "Mercury in Gemini",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "it thinks, reads four books at once, and learns anything fastest by explaining it to someone else within the hour. The phone is an extension of the nervous system — five texts where one would do, the asterisk correction, the link sent mid-conversation because it was relevant for four seconds. Waiting rooms are unbearable without reading material; silence gets filled on principle, usually charmingly. Strangers get interviewed in elevators. Every gathering yields one new fact, one new phrase, and at least one tangent that quietly became the actual topic. In conversation Conversation is this Mercury’s native sport, and it plays every position: opener, translator, the one who names the thing everyone was gesturing at. Questions come easily and the curiosity is genuine —"
