      "heading": "Mercury in Leo",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "communication guide → Asked and answered What does Mercury in Leo mean? Mercury handles thinking and talking; Leo turns both into performance. People with this placement think in stories, remember the arc and the punchline, and speak as if the room deserves their best take — because they believe it does. It isn’t vanity so much as a conviction that communication should be worth hearing. Do Mercury in Leo people exaggerate? They edit toward the better story — numbers rounded up, timelines tightened, the villain cast a little more vividly. The events are real; the color grading is theirs. If you need the raw footage, ask for it plainly and they’ll usually hand it over, slightly disappointed in you. Why is it hard for Mercury in Leo to admit being wrong? Because positions get announced here, not floated, and"
