      "text": "The texting tell is revision: the reply that arrives polished three minutes late, the ask cushioned in “no pressure at all.” The reflex phrase is “on the other hand,” and there is always another hand. Directions come as options: the fast way, the pretty way, and an honest accounting of both. How it weighs a decision For other people: instantly and well. This is the friend whose advice is genuinely balanced, the colleague who restates your argument better than you made it and then, if needed, dismantles it so courteously you thank them. For itself: committees. The same question goes out to three friends, the verdicts get averaged, and the average gets a second opinion. In an actual conflict, this Mercury keeps score of fairness rather than wins — it will concede a"
