      "text": "Placements ☿ Mercury in Pisces Classical standing fall In plain English Fall A traditional dignity label for a planet in the sign opposite its exaltation. A dignity is a traditional description of support, not a score for whether a placement is good or bad. Learn more about Fall → — the tradition’s uphill placement, strength earned rather than given Somewhere in the third tangent, the actual answer surfaces — sideways, dressed as an image, better than the direct route would have found it. Mercury in Pisces doesn’t walk to conclusions. It drifts to them, and the drift lands more often than anyone expects. How it shows up Mercury prefers labels, sequence, and clean handoffs; Pisces dissolves all three, and the old texts count this among the planet’s hardest assignments. You can hear it in the syntax — sentences that trail, restart, then"
