      "text": "Your birth chart shows the house where the weather gathers. Part of how your chart talks — the communication guide → Asked and answered What does Mercury in Pisces mean? Mercury is the chart’s thinking and talking; Pisces floods it with image, feeling, and atmosphere. This placement thinks associatively — by metaphor and drift rather than steps — and often arrives somewhere true by a route it can’t retrace. The style is gentle, funny in a sideways way, and hard to rush. Is Mercury in Pisces a bad placement? The old texts score Mercury lower here than anywhere else: it sits opposite Virgo, the seat of its sharpest sorting, so sequence, labels, and alphabetical anything run against the current. What that costs in logistics it repays in imagery and empathy. Poets and songwriters have been working that trade forever. Why do Mercury in"
