      "text": "friction: numbers rounded toward the story, dates remembered as eras, “basically” doing load-bearing work in every third sentence. What replaces precision is range. This mind connects the article to the trip to the argument to the book, and hands your own scattered facts back as a worldview. It learns by going — immersion, debate, the wrong train in a new country. Manuals go unread not from laziness but from format: context is the only container this mind trusts. In debate This placement debates for pleasure and means no harm by it, which it will explain, cheerfully, right after saying the true thing at the wrong volume. It persuades better than it proves: the sweep of the argument lands even when a supporting number turns out, on inspection, to have been a feeling. As a teacher, a coach, or the friend on a long walk, it’s"
