      "heading": "Mercury in Sagittarius",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "genuinely great — the one who makes your mess make sense from one story up. The bill arrives in the fine print it didn’t read, the name it rounded off, the article it forwarded on the strength of the headline. The growth edge Accuracy is a kind of honesty — the virtue this placement already prizes, applied one decimal further. The work is small: check the number before repeating it, say “roughly” when it’s roughly, let the boring middle of an explanation live. None of that shrinks the big picture; it licenses it. People trust the sweep more once the details spot-check clean. Review season is the built-in corrective. The Mercury retrograde calendar holds three windows a year — which is about how often this Mercury should reread something all the way through before forwarding it. Part of how your chart talks — the communication"
