      "heading": "Mercury in Taurus",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "it has touched over what it has read, which makes it nearly immune to hype and occasionally late to the news. The voice itself tends to be an asset — low, even, unhurried — the kind people describe as calming without being able to say why they told it so much. Books get finished here, one at a time, and quoted accurately a decade later. The growth edge Familiar and true are different categories, and this Mercury files them in one drawer. The work is scheduled revision: reopen one settled opinion a season and run it against current evidence. The placement evaluates beautifully — it just stops re-running the evaluation once the verdict starts to feel like furniture. A useful prompt: which settled view is oldest, and what has changed since it settled? On the calendar, the three Mercury retrograde windows each year suit this mind better than most; enforced double-checking is close to"
