      "heading": "Mercury in Virgo",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "Placements ☿ Mercury in Virgo Classical standing exaltation In plain English Exaltation A traditional dignity label meaning a planet is considered especially supported in that sign. A dignity is a traditional description of support, not a score for whether a placement is good or bad. Learn more about Exaltation → — the tradition’s honored-guest placement, working at its best The doubled word, the total that’s off by one, the plan with no step four — this mind catches them at rest, the way other people notice rain starting. Mercury in Virgo doesn’t hunt for errors; it simply cannot unsee them. How it shows up Mercury rules Virgo , and the old texts honor it here beyond any other sign — this is the planet’s processing side at full strength: sorting, editing, putting things to use. The learning style wants method — do it slowly and correctly"
