      "title": "Mercury in Virgo: precision as a first language",
      "heading": "Mercury in Virgo",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "not everyone owns the dictionary, and the placement forgets that unrequested edits read as verdicts. The people it goes over line by line are, reliably, the people it loves. The growth edge Aim. The editor is world-class; pointed at drafts, systems, and logistics, it’s a gift to everyone downstream. Pointed inward at 2 a.m., it becomes anxiety with a style guide — the sense that a life is a manuscript that has to be clean before anyone may see it. Done at 90 percent ships and survives; perfect at never doesn’t. And people aren’t paragraphs: most improve faster when the first comment isn’t a correction. Three weeks of enforced proofreading, three times a year, is the one discipline this placement already keeps — the Mercury retrograde calendar mostly tells everyone else when to start. Which house holds your Mercury decides what gets this"
