      "title": "Moon in Gemini: feelings that need words",
      "heading": "Moon in Gemini",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "a little more of it. The friend who gets the call isn’t being asked for solutions; they’re being asked to hold the other end of the sentence while the feeling takes shape. Moods here move like weather over a small state: quickly, and several times a day. What soothes is input — a walk with a podcast, a bookstore, a plan for next month, the right conversation at the right volume. Boredom is genuinely destabilizing for this placement, and restlessness is usually a request for new material, not evidence that the whole life is wrong. Home reflects that: books mid-read, tabs open, a radio talking to an empty kitchen. Silence is for sleeping. In relationships This Moon needs to be heard more than it needs to be helped. The processing is the conversation;"
