      "locale": "en",
      "text": "processing itself, happening out loud. Partners who stay in the conversation — and ask the second question, not just the first — get the real version. Do I need my birth time to know my Moon sign? The date alone answers it for about two birthdays in three. The Moon changes sign every two and a half days or so, which means the remaining third land on a boundary day where the hour decides. The Moon sign calculator tells you plainly if yours is one of them. Is this your Moon? Not sure this is your Moon? The calculator reads it from your birth date — and says honestly when the day is ambiguous. Find your moon sign ↗ Moon through the signs ← Taurus All placements Cancer → More in Gemini ☉ Sun ☿ Mercury ♀ Venus ♂ Mars ♃ Jupiter ♄ Saturn ♅ Uranus ♆ Neptune ♇ Pluto"
