      "heading": "Neptune in Cancer",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "Placements ♆ Neptune in Cancer Classical standing none — Neptune postdates the classical dignity system Home is already half memory and half invention; Neptune in Cancer makes it the whole horizon. This is a generational placement — Neptune gives each sign about 14 years, describing what an entire cohort idealizes, dissolves, and dreams in — so read the sign as an era’s mood and leave the individual work to the house and aspects. How it shows up Neptune floods the territory of Cancer : home, family, homeland, the past. The era’s shared dream becomes belonging — the kitchen everyone returns to, the country imagined as one family, the childhood remembered warmer than the thermometer recorded. A cohort born under it carries homesickness as a baseline mood, sometimes for places that never quite existed. The placement is archival for now; its people live"
