      "text": "previous cohort lies beyond the reach of living memory, and the next one begins arriving in 2038, when Neptune crosses into Taurus and — after one winter back in Aries — settles there until 2051. What it romanticizes, what it blurs The romance is the simple life: growing something, making something, owning little and touching everything. The blur is that “simple” is itself a luxury — the pastoral dream rarely includes the mud. Taurus fog also gathers around worth: a generation inclined to sanctify the tangible can mistake comfort for peace and possession for safety, the way other Neptune signs mistake belief for truth. The corrective is built into the sign. Actual ground, actual bread, actual hands — Taurus can always check the dream against the thing itself, and the best of this cohort will. In your own chart For now this placement lives in historical work: a great-great-"
