      "text": "belongs to a family’s eldest generation. Neptune does not re-enter Virgo until September 2092, settling in the following summer and holding the sign past 2100, where this site’s computed windows end. The dream of the useful life What it romanticizes: purity and competence — clean food, honest work, the fixable world. What the fog blurs: the difference between care and control, between improving yourself and erasing yourself. Virgo’s Neptune can sanctify worry, turning health into theology and service into disappearance. Its best expression is unglamorous by design: precise compassion, help that arrives on time and does not ask for applause. One note for the tables: Neptune holds no classical dignities in any sign, Virgo included — the friction here is temperamental, not doctrinal. In your own chart For living charts this is mostly ancestor work. The"
