      "text": "Placements ♇ Pluto in Sagittarius Classical standing none — Pluto postdates the classical dignity system Every Pluto generation inherits a question. The one born between 1995 and 2008 got a load-bearing one: what is worth believing, and who gets to say so? How it shows up Pluto crosses a sign in anywhere from 12 to 31 years — the orbit is lopsided — so its sign never describes a person. It describes a generation’s shared project, and leaves the personal reading to the house and aspects. This generation’s project is Sagittarius territory: belief, meaning, truth, and the distance between here and elsewhere. Pluto entered in January 1995, settled in that November, and left in January 2008, returning once from June to November of that year —"
