      "text": "Pluto first entered Scorpio on November 5, 1983, slid back into Libra from May to August 1984, then stayed through January 1995, with a final pass from April to November 1995. Nearly anyone born between those bookends carries it — the exceptions are that mid-1984 dip back into Libra and the gaps around the 1995 passes. Births in late 1983, mid-1984, or 1995 need a computed chart to settle which side they landed on. What does Pluto in Scorpio mean? It marks a generation rather than a personality: everyone born from late 1983 through 1995 shares it. What they share is a working familiarity with the material most eras keep buried — grief, desire, trust, the psyche. The house Pluto occupies in your chart shows where that depth actually operates for you. Does Pluto rule Scorpio? In modern astrology, yes. Classical"
