      "locale": "en",
      "text": "Placements ☉ Sun in Pisces Classical standing neutral — no special dignity In plain English Essential dignity A traditional system for describing how supported a planet is considered in a sign. Learn more about Essential dignity → here Every horoscope quietly assumes a firm line between you and not-you. Sun in Pisces makes that line optional. The edges of this identity are porous — moods, atmospheres, and other people’s unspoken weather cross them all day, in both directions — and everything the placement does well or badly starts there. How it shows up The Sun is the chart’s core self, and in Pisces the core is less a fortress than a tide pool, constantly refreshed by whatever washes in. You absorb moods before noticing them, read subtext as if it were printed, and imagine your way into other lives without trying — the"
