      "heading": "Sun in Pisces",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "stranger’s afternoon, the villain’s childhood, the coworker’s real reason. People experience this as uncanny empathy. From inside, it’s just the default resolution. The identity underneath is real; it’s simply responsive. A Pisces Sun can leave a two-hour dinner having been subtly someone else and need the drive home to change back. The full Pisces guide covers the sign end to end; the Sun’s own thread is this — a self whose gift and problem are the same permeable membrane. Keeping its own shape This Sun feels alive when the absorbed material becomes something: art, music, care work, chaplaincy of the official or unofficial kind, any craft that turns feeling into form. Imagination isn’t a luxury here — it’s the metabolism, and it runs whether or not it’s given work. Left unemployed, it manufactures dread with the same"
