      "heading": "Sun in Pisces",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "craftsmanship it would have given a novel. The drain is saturation: crowds without exits, jobs that demand all-day emotional reception, people who treat the open border as free infrastructure. None of that toughens this placement. It just fills it with material that was never yours to process. The growth edge Boundaries are not a betrayal of the gift; they are its maintenance. The unexamined version of this placement says yes by osmosis, disappears into whoever needs it most, and calls the resulting exhaustion love. The mature version schedules the closed door — solitude taken regularly, not as collapse but as sorting, until the borrowed moods drain off and what remains is recognizably you. That remainder was never as vague as everyone assumed; it just needed the tide out to be visible. Where the tide runs strongest —"
