      "text": "work, love, the twelfth house’s back rooms — depends on your Sun’s placement. Run your birth chart to see the house yours occupies, and which arena needs the most careful tending. Asked and answered What does Sun in Pisces mean? The Sun is core identity, and in Pisces its edges are porous: you absorb moods, read subtext as if it were printed, and imagine your way into other lives without trying. The identity underneath is real — it is simply responsive, tuned to whatever room it is in. Why don’t I feel like a Pisces? You may be feeling like whoever you’ve spent the week around — absorption is the placement’s signature move, and it applies to self-image too. The rising sign and Moon also front-load what you notice about yourself. The Pisces Sun is most visible in retrospect: in how much of other people’s weather you carried"
