      "title": "Sun in Sagittarius: aimed at the horizon",
      "heading": "Sun in Sagittarius",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "Placements ☉ Sun in Sagittarius Classical standing neutral — no special dignity In plain English Essential dignity A traditional system for describing how supported a planet is considered in a sign. Learn more about Essential dignity → here Of the twelve things a Sun can be, Sagittarius is the one that behaves most like an arrow: identity with a heading rather than an address. Where you are matters less to this placement than where all of this is going — and whether anyone plans to be honest about it along the way. How it shows up The Sun describes the project of a life, and in Sagittarius the project is distance: meaning, motion, and the honest version of every answer. This placement converts experience into worldview at speed — the trip becomes a theory, the disaster becomes a story with a moral, the stray fact"
