      "title": "Sun in Sagittarius: aimed at the horizon",
      "heading": "Sun in Sagittarius",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "becomes a thesis by Thursday. The famous bluntness isn’t carelessness; it’s a working belief that people deserve the real answer, delivered at the speed it was thought. The equally famous restlessness is easier to respect once you see what it’s for. The full Sagittarius guide covers the sign end to end; the Sun’s own signature there is simpler — an identity that stays alive by moving toward something larger than itself. What the restlessness is for This Sun charges on horizon: literal travel, yes, but also study, philosophy, foreign anything, the question behind the question. It needs a bigger picture the way other placements need security — a frame in which today’s absurdity means something. Teaching suits it unusually well; so does any work that turns experience into transmissible sense. The drain is low"
