      "text": "cost is the delay and the disguise. Handling things stands in for saying things — it fixes, provides, and calls that love, while the partner waits to be told in words. Work arrives first and warmth gets scheduled after deadlines, and the vetting that chose you can quietly keep running, so that some evenings feel like a review you didn’t know was on the calendar. The growth edge The work is letting love be unproductive. Not everything tender needs to be earned or useful; some of it just needs saying, out loud, at intervals a person can live on. The mature version discovers that the structure was always for someone — and lets that someone all the way inside it, on the record, ahead of schedule, while there are still plenty of years left to spend there together. Where the building happens depends on the"
