      "text": "pocket, the song sent at one in the morning that says what couldn’t quite be said in prose. The bill is the missing edges. Where you end and it begins can go unmarked until somebody is underwater; the placement can love a person’s potential so faithfully that it never quite meets the person actually in the room. Giving continues past empty and then calls the exhaustion devotion. And when reality gets loud, the vanishing act — fog, lateness, the unreachable week — stands in for the boundary it never set. The growth edge The work is discernment, practiced as a form of devotion: seeing what is actually there and loving that, at full strength, instead of the beautiful maybe. An edge is not the opposite of this love — it’s what keeps the supply from running out. The mature version still gives more than anyone; it just keeps a self on hand to give"
