      "text": "the mapped exit. Some part of this Venus always knows where the door is, and partners can feel the draft. Bluntness arrives unscheduled, promises made at full enthusiasm get revised at cruising altitude, and the word settle alarms it in both senses. The ordinary weeks — the ones with no departure in them — are where this placement’s commitment actually gets tested. The growth edge The work is putting the freedom inside the commitment instead of just beyond it. One person, fully explored, turns out to be a bigger country than it looked from the border. The mature version doesn’t stop leaving — it keeps choosing the same place to come back to, and finds that a window you return through beats a door you keep propped open, in every season worth staying for. Where"
