      "heading": "Aries rising",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "nothing is sent anywhere. Birth date Birth time Rising signs change every two hours — the clock matters here. Birthplace Search covers ~34,000 places · GeoNames (CC BY 4.0) Find your rising sign ↗ Private by default. Your birth details stay in this browser. Asked and answered What does Aries rising mean? Your rising sign is the sign that was climbing the eastern horizon when you were born — the chart's front door. With Aries there, you meet the world directly: quick to start, quick to speak, visibly readable. People tend to know where they stand with you inside a minute, whether or not that was the plan. What is the chart ruler for Aries rising? Mars. Whichever sign and house your Mars occupies becomes a second center of gravity for the whole chart — an Aries-rising person with Mars in Pisces leads with the charge but runs on tides. The computed panel on this"
