      "path": "/rising-sign/cancer/",
      "title": "Cancer Rising: shell first, welcome second",
      "heading": "Cancer rising",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "is the screen door — people can see warmth through it, but it stays latched until you decide otherwise. A Cancer rising over a Sagittarius sun greets you from behind that latch and, once you have been trusted, invites you on the road trip. When rising and sun differ this much, the rising decides the first hour and the sun decides the decade, and neither one was lying about you. The ascendant moves a sign roughly every two hours, so this reading rewards an accurate birth time. The calculator below takes your date, time, and place and computes the whole chart on your device, like everything here . Find your rising sign Birth date, time, and place — the ascendant needs all three. Computed on your device; nothing is sent anywhere. Birth date Birth time Rising signs change every two hours — the clock matters here. Birthplace Search covers ~34,000 places ·"
