      "text": "be generous, theatrical, and quietly delighted to be caught at it. If strangers call you stern and your oldest friends laugh at the description, the distance between those verdicts is your ascendant doing its job. Whether this rising is actually yours comes down to the clock: the ascendant moves a sign every two hours. The calculator just below settles it from your birth date, time, and place — nothing you enter leaves your device ( methodology ). Find your rising sign Birth date, time, and place — the ascendant needs all three. Computed on your device; nothing is sent anywhere. Birth date Birth time Rising signs change every two hours — the clock matters here. Birthplace Search covers ~34,000 places · GeoNames (CC BY 4.0) Find your rising sign ↗ Private by default. Your birth details stay in this browser. Asked and answered"
