      "locale": "en",
      "text": "What does Capricorn rising mean? Your rising sign is the sign that was climbing the eastern horizon when you were born — the manner the world meets before it meets you. With Capricorn there, you arrive composed: measured pace, level voice, an air of having already read the agenda. Strangers routinely assume you're in charge, and rooms hand you responsibility on sight. What is the chart ruler for Capricorn rising? Saturn. Whichever sign and house your Saturn occupies becomes the chart's second anchor — a Capricorn rising with Saturn in Taurus builds slowly out of solid material and keeps what it builds, while one with Saturn in Gemini disciplines the mind instead: lists, drafts, exact words. Saturn's condition shows where the real work of the chart lives. How is Capricorn rising different from a Capricorn sun? The sun is what"
