      "heading": "Aries and Capricorn",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "misreadings are predictable. Capricorn’s deliberateness lands on Aries as refusal — every plan met with a stress test, every yes wearing a not yet . Aries’ launches land on Capricorn as maintenance debt — engines revved without oil, headed somewhere expensive. Under the friction, though, runs a current of real respect: Capricorn has watched a hundred people talk and one person start, and Aries is the one. Aries has watched a hundred people start and one person finish. In love Capricorn loves structurally: the car serviced, the crisis absorbed before you saw it coming, a future designed with you already in it. It doesn’t audition for anything it isn’t prepared to keep, so the opening tempo gap is real — Aries announces early and often, Capricorn verifies twice before announcing anything. The translation work"
