      "locale": "en",
      "text": "runs both ways. Aries learns that maintenance is a love language, spoken fluently and daily. Capricorn learns that the people being quietly handled sometimes need the sentence said in actual words — and that Aries, of all partners, will never mock the saying of it. It helps that Capricorn turns out to be the funniest person Aries has ever met — deadpan, mid-crisis, without a change of expression — and that Aries laughs at full volume every time, which Capricorn files, privately, as a reason to keep going. Where it grinds The recurring fight is tempo dressed up as respect. Aries begins to feel managed — a junior partner whose ideas require sign-off, whose speed is treated as a liability to be governed. Capricorn begins to feel used as the brake — cast permanently as the gray one, invited along only to say not"
