      "text": "kind, and the entire will-they phase is settled inside a week. Neither partner plays the anchor, checks the other’s location, or reads commitment as confinement — and for two people who have each fled relationships over exactly that, the relief is enormous. Jealousy never really gets oxygen: each has a horizon of their own, which is precisely what makes the other stay. The Archer keeps a partner who would rather come along than hold on; Aries keeps one who stays slightly out ahead, permanently worth chasing. Where it grinds The boring middle, and who is going to live in it. Neither wants to hold ground: the lease renewal, the insurance call, the plan’s unglamorous third month. Two overbooked calendars generate more enthusiasm than any week can honor, and the promises that slip first are the ones to each other — each quietly assuming the"
