      "heading": "Aries and Scorpio",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "hooks in the compliments. And Scorpio’s total, undivided attention gives Aries something applause never quite was: being genuinely seen, at depth, and chosen anyway. When Scorpio commits, it is complete and private; when Aries commits, it is complete and audible. Between the two, the coverage is total. Where it grinds The record fight. An Aries eruption is over — for Aries — by dinner. For Scorpio it enters the archive, and the archive has no delete key. So a flare from two years ago surfaces, verbatim, in the middle of an unrelated Tuesday disagreement, and Aries feels prosecuted for a crime they’d honestly forgotten committing, while Scorpio can’t fathom how the other person forgot . To one of them, forgetting is mercy; to the other, it’s proof the thing never mattered. The second grind is trials."
