      "heading": "Leo and Sagittarius",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "monthly until somebody names it. The quieter grind is geography. Leo holds ground — the home, the court, the standing Sunday dinner; Sagittarius keeps widening the map. Too many solo departures and Leo feels unchosen. Too much required attendance and somewhere, quietly, a Sagittarius countdown starts. Neither drift is malicious; both are load-bearing habits. What makes it last Aim, and a good landing strip. Sagittarius learns that the same truth delivered privately is a gift and delivered publicly is an arrow — for this partner, timing isn’t dishonesty, it’s marksmanship. Leo learns that the teasing is Sagittarius loyalty in native dress: this sign only bothers being precise about people it loves, and it’s also the one partner who’ll tell Leo the truth nobody else will risk. Then build a calendar with both kinds of"
