      "text": "events on it — departures and returns. Let Sagittarius go without a hearing; let Leo make the coming-home an occasion, because it will anyway. Nothing keeps an Archer like a home that beats the trip, and nothing suits a Lion like being the reason somebody keeps crossing the world to get back. Why this pairing reads this way Elements, modes, polarity, and each sign’s basic pattern Leo Jul 23 – Aug 22 Fire · Fixed · Sun Sagittarius Nov 22 – Dec 21 Fire · Mutable · Jupiter Elements Shared heat Two fire signs move at the same speed and forgive at the same speed. The open question is who minds the brakes. Modes Anchor and sail Stability plus flexibility, each supplying what the other skips — resented only when either denies the other’s function. Polarity Both day signs: energy runs outward on both sides, toward action and"
