      "heading": "Leo and Scorpio",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "not cheat, and resents being asked to prove it. Both keep the grievance afterward; one files it, one enthrones it. The standoffs are long, regal, and cold, and each partner is privately certain the other will fold first. Neither ever has. What makes it last Jurisdictions, negotiated in advance. Decide together what’s public and what’s under seal — the anniversary yes, the argument no, the family matter never — so the boundary becomes a treaty instead of a weekly ambush at the dinner table. Then each pays the other’s toll. Scorpio says the devotion out loud sometimes, with witnesses, because for Leo a love that’s never declared never feels entirely real. Leo keeps a few things only-theirs — the inside joke that stays inside, the story that never gets told — because for Scorpio, secrecy is intimacy, not shame. Each"
