      "heading": "Leo and Virgo",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "Meanwhile Virgo’s work is invisible by design, so nobody is clapping for the fixer either. Two people, both under-thanked, each holding the other’s exact remedy. What makes it last Translation, practiced until fluent. Leo learns that a quietly serviced life is a standing ovation in Virgo’s language — the love was in the details the whole time. Virgo learns to deliver notes privately, lead with what worked, and say the praise out loud even when it feels redundant, because to Leo, unspoken admiration doesn’t exist. Then each makes the high-value move. Leo names Virgo’s invisible work in front of people — the credit Virgo would never request and never forgets. Virgo lets one imperfect evening stand uncorrected, because the host was happy and that mattered more than the seating chart. Give them a shared"
