      "locale": "en",
      "text": "pairings, is mostly absent from this one, and both partners notice the quiet. The real difference is thermal. Libra warms to whatever room it’s in, mood synced to the company. Aquarius runs its own thermostat from a few hundred miles up. One partner is calibrated to the collective weather; the other is largely exempt from it. In love Friendship-first is Aquarius’s non-negotiable sequence and Libra’s natural habitat, so the beginning suits them both: long conversations that keep refusing to end, affection accumulating under cover of debate. Aquarius never tries to own, dim, or manage Libra — after partners who kept score, that restraint lands like open air. Libra, meanwhile, gives Aquarius a warmer and better-composed life than the Water-Bearer would ever build alone, without once asking it to become conventional. The lag is the"
