      "locale": "en",
      "text": "hard part. Aquarius’s affection arrives on a delay, and often in described form — “I notice I’ve missed you” — while Libra, calibrated to responsiveness, can spend that delay quietly searching itself for the fault. The fault usually isn’t there. The delay is just the distance the signal travels from orbit, and it tends to arrive carrying more warmth than its timing suggests. Where it grinds The dinner-party principle. Aquarius states the unpopular position, serenely, and declines to soften it for the table. Libra, whose comfort requires level ground, does damage control in real time and resents the assignment. The fight afterward is the recurring one: Libra calls the provocation needless; Aquarius calls the smoothing a small dishonesty; and each is defending its foundation — harmony as the point of gathering, truth as the point of"
