      "text": "keeping a precise unspoken record of every empty chair. When it finally surfaces, the styles collide too. Libra needs the graceful fight: both sides heard, fairness visible, tone intact. Capricorn runs conflict like a project review — blunt, itemized, closed by end of meeting. Libra hears coldness; Capricorn hears a negotiation that refuses to land. And beneath it all, the decision tempo grates: Capricorn settled in March the question Libra is still weighing in June. What makes it last Putting the dinners in the plan. Capricorn honors whatever it has classified as load-bearing, so the fix is classification: the Thursday table, the anniversary, the friends’ wedding go in as commitments with the same standing as anything at work — and then they simply happen, because Capricorn does not miss commitments. Libra, in turn, learns to submit"
