      "text": "Pisces turns them into mythology; both would rather believe generously than double-check. Neither keeps score, neither sweats the small stuff, and the household has a porous, welcoming, slightly unmoored quality that guests never want to leave. Chores are another matter — but neither partner ever pretended otherwise, and the important things somehow get done the night before. In love Pisces falls completely and paints the portrait a shade better than life; Sagittarius, constitutionally optimistic, sees no reason not to live up to it. It’s romance with the volume up — devotion from one side, adventure from the other, laughter from both. Pisces gives the Archer what blunt company never has: an imagination that keeps pace with the appetite. Sagittarius gives the Fish a horizon outside its own"
