      "text": "pressures anybody, which both experience as courtship. The affection runs on different frequencies — Taurus transmits through touch and food, Aquarius through ideas, loyalty, and decades of showing up — and both signals are real. Learning to receive the other’s is the early work, and it’s worth doing early. Where it grinds Closeness itself. Taurus wants presence: the shared evening, the body in the room, the ritual intact. Aquarius needs orbit: protected solitude, separate hobbies, a life that never fully merges. So Taurus reaches, and Aquarius steps back precisely when reached for; the Bull reads the step as coldness and grips; the grip confirms Aquarius’s suspicion that closeness costs edges. Around it goes. Neither need is fake — the Bull genuinely runs on shared warmth, Aquarius genuinely runs on air — and it only"
