      "heading": "Taurus and Aquarius",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "turns cruel when each starts reading the other’s need as a verdict on itself. The recurring fight is change proposed as improvement. Aquarius redesigns a domestic ritual — sincerely, as an upgrade — and Taurus receives the redesign as an attack on home itself. Neither yields, both are certain, and these two can run the same polite argument for ten years without noticing it’s the same argument. What makes it last A treaty with two permanent clauses — permanence being the one aesthetic they share. First: some things don’t get redesigned. Taurus names them, Aquarius signs, and Sunday becomes constitutional. Second: the orbit is not a symptom. Aquarius’s solitude gets treated as maintenance, never as a loyalty question. Underneath sits the thing they rarely credit each other with: neither leaves. Aquarius keeps its people"
