      "text": "stopped trusting you is already leaving, however still it’s standing. Gemini, meanwhile, feels charged with a crime it can’t see: nothing was canceled, things merely improved. The second grind is boredom, Gemini’s only real enemy. Left restless too long, it starts poking at the beloved routine just to watch it move, and Taurus hears every poke as a review of the life it built. What makes it last Two calendars in one household. A fixed spine of standing plans that do not move — Taurus’s floor, non-negotiable — surrounded by open space Gemini may rearrange freely and without appeal. Gemini learns that a kept Tuesday buys enormous trust with a Bull; Taurus learns that a changed plan flagged early is not a broken promise, just a plan with better information in it. What each gets is what neither could self-supply. Gemini"
