      "text": "running well is warm, generous, and faintly regal: everything celebrated, everything maintained. Friends learn to answer invitations early, because the parties — Leo’s sense of occasion, Taurus’s cooking — end with guests sent home carrying leftovers and compliments. Both are proud, both are certain, and neither repositions once planted. When they agree, that doubled certainty is formidable — this couple finishes what it starts and defends what it builds. When they disagree, nothing in the house moves for months, including the conversation. In love Leo is drawn to the one audience it can’t dazzle. A slow nod from Taurus is worth a standing ovation from anyone else, and Leo — oversupplied with ovations — finds the nod addictive. Taurus, for its part, rather likes being treated royally:"
