      "heading": "Taurus and Leo",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "was wrong with the perfectly good evening. Leo feels uncelebrated. Taurus feels uncounted — as if a decade of showing up doesn’t register because it never came with a toast. Then the second problem arrives: neither backs down. The same fight can run quarterly for years, nearly word for word, because both partners would rather hold the position than hand the other the win. Pride plus patience makes an extremely durable deadlock. What makes it last Paying in the other’s currency, on purpose. Taurus stands up at the dinner and says the proud thing in front of the friends — one sentence, and Leo runs on it for a month. Leo learns to count ten years of Tuesdays as the standing ovation they are, delivered one quiet evening at a time. The reward for learning the exchange is the thing both wanted all"
