      "locale": "en",
      "text": "Libra sometimes agrees in the room to keep the evening level, then reopens the agreement later, once the jury inside finishes. Taurus took the agreement literally and poured concrete on it. The reopening lands as a moved goalpost — the Bull’s exact allergy — while Libra, who was never lying, just still deliberating, feels punished for being thorough. What makes it last Deadlines for the scales, labels from the Bull. Libra agrees that verdicts land by a named date — deciding is also a fairness, owed to the person waiting. Taurus agrees to flag which of its pronouncements are actually final, and to reopen one now and then as a gift, because some of Libra’s late evidence is genuinely good. The couple that builds both habits stops relitigating the sofa by year two. Underneath the procedure, the fit is real. Libra"
