      "locale": "en",
      "text": "never slams a door. Virgo wants to be needed without being used, and Libra, who genuinely weighs what’s owed on both sides of any arrangement, is the sign least likely to take the help and forget who carried it. Where it grinds The recurring fight is about what gets said, and when. Virgo states what it notices, in the moment, with timestamps. Libra hears a steady drizzle of small verdicts in a home that was supposed to be a refuge, and responds the way Libra responds to friction: by smoothing it — agreeing in the room, disagreeing in the car. Weeks later Virgo discovers the agreement was decorative and feels managed, which for a sign that runs on accurate information is the deepest cut available. Each is protecting something real. Virgo is guarding the truth of the household; Libra is guarding the peace of it; and each keeps"
