      "heading": "Virgo and Pisces",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "the other’s missing half in the old, satisfying way. Virgo keeps the dream from dissolving into the scroll and the nap; Pisces keeps the fixer from becoming the fixing. The portrait and the fine print, finally in the same frame — and both of them, on a good evening, know exactly how lucky that is. Why this pairing reads this way Elements, modes, polarity, and each sign’s basic pattern Virgo Aug 23 – Sep 22 Earth · Mutable · Mercury Pisces Feb 19 – Mar 20 Water · Mutable · Neptune Elements River and bank Water softens earth and earth gives water shape — the classic quiet-strength pairing, genuinely low-friction. Modes Two sails Endlessly adaptable and rarely in open conflict. Decisions can orbit for months without landing; name a deadline. Polarity Both night signs: both process inward before anything"
