      "text": "declares itself early and means it. It wants a peer, not a project — someone mid-mission in their own right who admires openly and competes lightly. Respect lands better than flattery. At work the Sun-decan pattern is ownership: hand an April 1 the hard problem and the byline and they’ll carry both; hand them a committee and a shared inbox and the light goes out. They lead well because going first into the unproven thing genuinely doesn’t scare them. When the spark skips the check The friction is pride on a hair trigger. A date that spends every birthday braced for jokes can learn to hear mockery in ordinary correction, and mid-Aries acts on the hearing before verifying it. The growth is one beat of delay: let the comment land, decide"
