      "heading": "Born on April 2",
      "locale": "en",
      "text": "top of Mars fuel, and one of the steadiest cuts of a famously unsteady sign. The Sun behind the Ram The Aries Sun is an identity built on forward motion, and in this decan the motion picks up dignity. April 2 people don’t just want to act; they want the action to stand for something and to be done in their own name. There’s a natural generosity here — credit shared downward, newcomers championed — alongside a quiet assumption of the center seat. Not arrogance, exactly. More the unexamined belief that someone has to go first, and it may as well be them. Voices like this get called bossy young and indispensable later. Devotion out loud Love, for this birthday, is a public commitment rather than a private arrangement:"
