      "locale": "en",
      "text": "this one starts fresh on solid ground — a quietly enviable position on the calendar. Earth, newly arrived Day-one Taurus is the sign at its most literal: settle, taste, build. The Taurus Sun here hasn’t acquired the later sign’s elaborations — it wants good meals, kept promises, a bed worth returning to, and the time to enjoy each without a countdown running. There’s a freshness to this cut of the Bull: the steadiness hasn’t hardened into doctrine yet, and curiosity about comfort — new recipes, new routes to calm — stays genuinely open. People find April 21 restful the way an unhurried room is restful: nothing is being performed, and the ease turns out to be structural. Slow love, sound work Affection here moves at ground speed: interest, then attention, then"
