      "text": "Water that learns the banks A Pisces Sun doesn’t resist the river; it studies it. What reads as luck from outside is actually rapid, mostly unconscious recalibration — sensing the new rules of a room before anyone explains them, adjusting without announcing it. Jupiter’s tone adds appetite: change isn’t just survivable here, it’s interesting. February 24 is the friend who moved abroad with two suitcases and was somehow local by June. Easy to live with, hard to pin In love the flexibility is a gift with a clause. This date accommodates beautifully — schedules, quirks, in-laws — and makes a famously easy partner; pinning it to a five-year plan is the struggle, since every plan feels like a wall pretending the river stopped. It pairs best with someone decisive enough to propose a direction and relaxed enough to revise it. At work, flux is the habitat: startups, turnarounds,"
