      "text": "March 30 typically does both: the blunt opening question, then, unexpectedly, the anniversary remembered with theater. At work the blend suits arenas that need both launch and reign — founding a thing and then actually fronting it, opening the restaurant and hosting its floor, starting the practice and keeping its patients for decades. Pride and impatience, twin risks Each decan ships its hazard. Mars-side, it’s impatience — the fuse, the leap, the bruise. Sun-side, it’s pride — the need to be seen winning, the difficulty of apologizing while lit. On a hinge date both are worth watching, since either can take the front on a given day. The common cure is cheaper than it sounds: one breath between impulse and act, one between slight and reply. The Aries guide"
