      "text": "The early diplomat A Libra Sun this fresh in the sign hasn’t learned to hide the instinct: September 27 hears both sides at full volume, finds the sentence both parties can sign, and treats a well-brokered agreement the way painters treat a finished canvas. The talent is craft, not niceness — watch one turn a dispute into a decision without anyone losing face, and count the moves. There were more than you saw. Their sentences are built for two audiences at once, and both walk away feeling they won something. The art of the alliance Romantically, September 27 courts like it negotiates, in the best sense: attentive to what matters to you, generous by default, intent on a pairing both people would re-choose. It needs conflict handled with civility —"
